        "type": "text",
        "timescale": "day",
        "version": 2,
        "content": "<h2>Fancier Device List</h2><p>Link to source: <a href=\"https://github.com/logicmonitor/custom_widgets/blob/main/sdk/examples/device-list-widget2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" id=\"isPasted\"><span style=\"color: rgb(247, 218, 100);\">device_list_widget2.html</span></a></p><p id=\"isPasted\">A more elaborate example of a LogicMonitor Text/Custom HTML widget using the LogicMonitor Widget SDK.</p><p>This widget will display a table of devices in alert status (i.e. alert status is something other than &quot;none&quot;), with columns for a colored icon indicating the highest severity for each device, the device name, and its system info. Each device name will be a link to the device&#39;s alert details page. It will also show a summary of the number of devices in alert status and the number of alerts that have not cleared.</p><p>SDK commands this script helps demonstrate:</p><ul><li>lm.auth.fromTokens()</li><li>lm.configure()</li><li>lm.context.injectStyle()</li><li>lm.context.onReady()</li><li>lm.error()</li><li>lm.escapeHtml()</li><li>lm.getAlerts()</li><li>lm.getProperty()</li><li>lm.getStatusColor()</li><li>lm.info()</li><li>lm.query()</li></ul>"
