        "content": "<h2>Section Header</h2><p>Link to source: <a href=\"https://github.com/logicmonitor/custom_widgets/blob/main/src/Dashboard_Header_Widget.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"color: rgb(247, 218, 100);\">Dashboard_Header_Widget.html</span></a></p><p id=\"isPasted\">What this example does:</p><ul><li>Hides the widget&#39;s background so it blends seamlessly with the dashboard itself.</li><li>Enlarges the widget&#39;s title so it can act as the section header (the text in the widget body can be used for extra detail).</li><li>Adds a bottom border to the widget so it&#39;s visually separated from the widgets below it.</li><li>Adds a hover effect to the widget so it&#39;s easy to tell when the widget is being hovered over.</li><li>Watches for size changes and resizes the widget to fit its content.</li></ul><p id=\"isPasted\">SDK functions demonstrated:</p><ul><li><strong>lm.context.onReady</strong> - wait for the widget to finish rendering.</li><li><strong>lm.context.widgetContainer</strong> / <strong>widgetTitle</strong> / <strong>widgetParent</strong> / <strong>widgetFrame</strong> - locate the widget&#39;s elements in the dashboard.</li><li><strong>lm.context.setStyleIfChanged</strong> - change inline styles without triggering needless layout cycles.</li><li><strong>lm.context.injectParentStyle</strong> - add CSS to the dashboard page (the widget card lives outside this iframe).</li><li><strong>lm.context.injectStyle</strong> - add CSS to this widget&#39;s own content.</li><li><strong>lm.context.observeSize</strong> - react to size changes (throttled to once per animation frame).</li><li><strong>lm.context.fitFrameToContent</strong> / <strong>resizeFrame</strong> - size the iframe to match its content (growing and shrinking).</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>"
